lines=['# Postgame model analysis — September 28–29, 2026','',f"Written {d['created_at_utc']}. Dates use America/Los_Angeles. Frozen forecasts only; current finals are outcomes, never retroactive model inputs.",'','## September 28 — NFL','', '**Final: Chicago 27, Philadelphia 7.** The primary is the last eligible frozen Keenum-condition version (September 28, 4:56 p.m. Pacific), with end-of-Week-2 state. Earlier Monday versions and Williams/Bagent counterfactuals are not substituted or pooled. The already-recorded Monday research grade is referenced; no duplicate was appended.','', '| Product | Frozen model | Frozen simulation | Market no-vig | Actual / interpretation |','|---|---:|---:|---:|---|',f"| PHI outright | {pct(n['phi_win']['p'])} | {pct(n['phi_win_simulation']['p'])} | {pct(n['market_phi_win']['p'])} | Lost; winner direction wrong |",f"| PHI −3.5 | {pct(n['phi_cover_minus3_5']['p'])} | {pct(n['phi_cover_simulation_p'])} | {pct(n['market_phi_cover']['p'])} | Did not cover; model favored CHI +3.5 |",f"| Expected PHI margin | +{n['mean_phi_margin']:.2f} | +2.36 | Market spread PHI −3.5 | Actual −20; absolute error {n['absolute_margin_error']:.2f} points |",'','The separate calibrated integer-margin arm is `nfl.qb_margin.integer_blend.v1.research`; the winner arm is `nfl.integrated_context.qb.v1.research`. Its margin distribution is not a joint-score model. No supported total/score forecast was graded.','',f"Winner Brier: **{n['phi_win']['brier']:.4f} model vs {n['market_phi_win']['brier']:.4f} market**, delta {n['phi_win']['brier']-n['market_phi_win']['brier']:+.4f}. Spread Brier: **{n['phi_cover_minus3_5']['brier']:.4f} vs {n['market_phi_cover']['brier']:.4f}**, delta {n['phi_cover_minus3_5']['brier']-n['market_phi_cover']['brier']:+.4f}. Lower is better; a losing favorite forecast can score better than a more confident losing market forecast. One event establishes no calibration advantage.",'',f"The actual margin was outside the central 80% interval (PHI −15 to +19). The frozen law assigned **{pct(n['probability_chi_win_by_at_least20'])}** to Chicago winning by at least 20. This was a tail outcome, not a zero-probability event.",'', 'The official Bears recap reports Keenum 24/34 for 247 yards, two passing touchdowns and no interceptions, plus a rushing touchdown. Chicago forced three turnovers; Philadelphia was 2/9 on third down and gained 62 second-half yards. The model used the correct starting-QB condition. The miss concerns the resulting team performance and game distribution, not an accidental Williams assumption. These observations support the existing turnover and QB-uncertainty research queue; they do not identify a causal coefficient adjustment from one game.','', 'Official recap: https://www.chicagobears.com/news/game-recap-case-keenum-defense-lead-bears-to-dominant-victory-over-eagles','', 'Market benchmark was captured at 23:58:31Z, after the model freeze and before kickoff: PHI −198 / CHI +164, PHI −3.5 at −112 / CHI +3.5 at −108. The later total was 42.5; the earlier screenshot’s 41.5 is a different version. Market settlement terms remain unverified, so comparisons are diagnostic, with no ROI or payout grade. Official-gamebook clearance is still false. Weather was imputed and non-QB availability was not numerically consumed.','', '## September 29 — NHL','', 'Winner probabilities below name the model’s favored team. Model / simulation percentages are from retained 100,000-draw runs, not postgame reruns. All five official NHL finals reconcile to ESPN.','', '| Game | Final | Original winner-only model / sim | Joint-score model / sim | Joint timing cohort |','|---|---|---|---|---|']
