ss=s['strict_joint3'];lines += [f"For the three timing-eligible joint forecasts: winner **2/3, Brier {ss['joint_winner']['brier']:.4f}**; quoted puck-line direction **2/3, Brier {ss['quoted_cover']['brier']:.4f}**; quoted totals **1/3, Brier {ss['quoted_total']['brier']:.4f}**.",'',f"The predeclared primary is **home −1.5**, not whichever quoted side happens to look best. Its Brier is **{ss['joint_primary_home_minus1_5']['brier']:.4f}** versus **{ss['unconditional_home_minus1_5']['brier']:.4f}** for the frozen 7,428-game unconditional settled-margin pool; delta **{ss['delta_primary_minus_baseline_brier']:+.4f}**. Baseline P(home wins by 2+)={pct(s['baseline_home_minus1_5'])}. Log loss is {ss['joint_primary_home_minus1_5']['log_loss']:.4f} versus {ss['unconditional_home_minus1_5']['log_loss']:.4f}. This is three observations in one ISO week, far short of the registered 500-game / eight-week minimum. Week-bootstrap inference would be degenerate; no confidence or promotion conclusion is warranted.",'','### Error breakdown','', '- **Montreal–Toronto:** original MTL direction was correct; joint TOR direction was wrong. Toronto +1.5 nevertheless covered. Winner and cover are different events. The late-registered row is not allowed to improve or worsen the strict prospective record.','- **Vancouver–Edmonton:** both arms favored Edmonton; the joint arm reduced Edmonton from 71.50% to 61.46% but still missed the winner. Vancouver +1.5 covered. The 11-goal final exceeded the frozen central-80% total interval; only 6.963% of retained draws had at least 11 goals. This is a total-tail miss, not proof that the model forecast a Vancouver upset.','- **New York–Boston:** both winner directions and BOS +1.5 were correct; over 5.5 missed with only three goals. Official PBP records one Boston empty-net goal. Boston already led by two before it, so that goal did not flip ±1.5 settlement.','- **Chicago–Vegas:** both winner directions were correct, but CHI +1.5 failed. Vegas already led 4–2 before its empty-net goal made it 5–2; the empty-net goal did not cause the puck-line miss. Over 5.5 was correct.','- **Florida–Carolina:** the original CAR direction missed in a 1–0 overtime game. No joint forecast was issued after the event had started.','', 'Descriptive slices are retained in analysis.json: one-goal versus multi-goal games, OT versus regulation, empty-net presence, market-favorite strength, and 5.5 versus 6.5 total environments. Every subgroup has only one to three joint observations. Observed goalie and player performance is postgame evidence; neither model consumed a registered player-availability/goalie-effect increment for these forecasts. Do not backfill those inputs into the frozen versions.','', 'Official result sources: https://api-web.nhle.com/v1/schedule/2026-09-29 and the five linked gamecenter PBP/boxscore captures in source-receipts.json / detail-receipts.json. Empty-net flags require the opposing goalie-absence position of situationCode; a team scoring with its own goalie pulled is not an empty-net goal.','', '## Coverage and operational limits','', '- September 28: NFL PHI–CHI was the only event in the seven-league captured census.','- September 29: MLB playoff finals ATL 5–3 PHI, CWS 6–3 HOU, NYY 9–0 BOS, SD 8–0 CHC; WNBA playoff finals IND 99–89 LVA and NYL 87–71 MIN. No supported frozen forecasts were located for those postseason products, so model grades are N/A. Results are not predictions.','- CFB/NBA/MLS had no events in either date’s captured provider census; NFL had no September 29 event. September 30/October 1 NHL forecasts are outside this report and remain ungraded.','- This is an additive postgame audit, not a canonical universal grader or a weekly-state transition. NFL’s prior research grade remains single-counted. NHL research rows are durable audit evidence; the canonical grading ledger and old prospective-ledger bytes are untouched.','- 27 source captures succeeded. All 75 original NHL registry file hashes matched. Four retained joint draw arrays and the Monday margin draw hash were verified; no forecast rerun or coefficient update was performed.','- Local healthcheck exited 1 with 11 failures and six warnings, including snapshot/environment limitations and unresolved historical/recovery gates. This does not grant official release or gamebook clearance. See the retained health log; tests are not predictive validation.','', '## Findings and next evidence','', '| Issue | Fixed / established | Not established / remaining | Next evidence |','|---|---|---|---|','| POST-0928-QB-TAIL | Correct Keenum-conditioned primary and actual result bound | Why QB/team forecast underestimated Chicago; one result cannot identify coefficients | Official gamebook reconciliation; frozen contribution decomposition; turnover study on dev/held-out cohorts |','| POST-0929-ARM-DIVERGENCE | Paired original/joint scores calculated on identical IDs | Joint winner improvement is not established; four-game score is worse | Continue registered prospective cohort; keep arms separate |','| POST-0929-SETTLEMENT | Official full-game finals and OT/EN labels captured | Exact screenshot sportsbook/jurisdiction/time binding | Authenticated original market record and applicable rules before market eligibility |','| POST-0929-TOTAL-TAIL | VAN–EDM total-tail miss quantified from frozen draws | Calibration or personnel improvement | Accumulate prospective reliability/tail slices; separate goalie/availability challenger increment |','| POST-0929-LATE-ARCHIVE | Montreal excluded from strict timing cohort | No retroactive repair can make it timely | Complete future immutable publication before the declared cutoff |','', 'These are linked audit findings, not claims that canonical standing-health cards were changed or their aging reset. Reproducibility: source-byte reconciliation plus frozen-artifact scoring; official-release eligibility remains false.','', 'Keep the original winner-only arm and joint-score challenger separate. Continue prospective scoring under the existing protocol; no retraining, blending, state transition or wagering change follows from this small batch. **Action OFF; dose 0.0.**','']
